      "urpx:forRatePlan": {
        "@id": "sdge:dr-ses"
      },
      "urpx:hasCoverageClaim": {
        "@id": "sdge:cc-dr-ses-2026-09-30",
        "@type": "urpx:CoverageClaim",
        "urpx:completenessResult": {
          "@id": "urpx:partial"
        },
        "urpx:selfContained": true,
        "urpx:explainedBy": {
          "@type": "urpx:Evaluation",
          "@id": "sdge:cc-dr-ses-2026-09-30-evaluation",
          "urpx:evaluationKind": {
            "@id": "urpx:coverageEvaluation"
          },
          "urpx:description": "This filing does not carry everything its source document states. 5 parts are deferred, listed here in the same words as the filing's tariff.toml [modeling].deferrals so the two records cannot drift. (1) Franchise Fee Differential of 5.78 percent on the monthly billings calculated under this schedule, for customers inside the corporate limits of the City of San Diego. Source: Sheet 5, Original Cal. P.U.C. Sheet No. 65156-E, Advice 4874-E, under the heading Franchise Fee Differential. Not a vocabulary gap under v0.5.1: express it as a Price carrying urpx:multiplier 0.0578 and urpx:basedOnPrice naming a urpx:PriceSummary over this filing's own charges, chargeType urpx:taxMunicipal, gated on urpx:hasMunicipality in a ConditionExpression. This filing already carries two working PriceSummary nodes for the CARE and FERA discounts, so the subtotal machinery exists. Unbuilt: no SDG&E filing in this corpus prices it. Before building it, note that the ConditionExpression carries the whole of the restriction: a Price that does not carry it, or a consumer that does not evaluate it, applies the 5.78 percent to every DR-SES customer, most of whom are outside the city, trading a known omission for a confident wrong number. (2) Medical Baseline customers on DR-SES are not billed the California Wildfire Fund Non-Bypassable Charge, so the $0.00591 per kWh WF-NBC this filing carries is not billed to them. Source: Sheet 4, Original Cal. P.U.C. Sheet No. 65155-E, which shows the Wildfire Non-Bypassable Charge and the DWR Bond Charge as N/A in the DR-SES-MB column; the DWR-BC half is moot because its rate is 0.00000. Sheet 2 (Original Cal. P.U.C. Sheet No. 65153-E) also prints a DR-SES-MB Total Effective Energy Rates column, which its note 2 calls illustrative and attributes to discounts under Schedule E-MEDICAL: each cell is 80 percent of the DR-SES-MB Total Energy Rate beside it, for example $0.59482 against $0.74353 summer on-peak for bundled customers. The DR-SES-MB Base Services Charge is the standard $0.79343 per day. The WF-NBC exemption is expressible now and already precedented in this corpus: the SDG&E CARE overlay at us/ca/sdge/electricity/care/versions/2025-10-01/ carries sdge:care-price-wf-nbc-exemption-2025-10-01 at -0.00591 and lists sdge:dr-ses in urpx:applicableToRatePlan, so the identical shape works for Medical Baseline. Unbuilt because this corpus holds no SDG&E Medical Baseline overlay at all (SCE has one at us/ca/sce/electricity/medical-baseline/; SDG&E has none) and Schedule E-MEDICAL, which General Special Condition 15 cites, is not in this repo. (3) SDG&E Electric Rule 1 (DEFINITIONS), Sheet 6, Cal. P.U.C. Sheet No. 61672-E, HOLIDAYS: \"When a Holiday listed above falls on Sunday, the following Monday shall be defined as a Holiday. No change will be made for Holidays falling on Saturday.\" New Year's Day, Independence Day, Veterans Day and Christmas Day in sdge:dr-ses-2026-09-30-holidays carry no urpx:observanceRule, so each resolves on its actual date and a Saturday one stays on Saturday. The Monday after a Sunday New Year's Day, Independence Day, Veterans Day or Christmas Day is carried as a dated urpx:Holiday with urpx:holidayDate: 2027-07-05, 2029-11-12, 2032-07-05, 2033-12-26, 2034-01-02, 2035-11-12, 2038-07-05, 2039-12-26, 2040-01-02 and 2040-11-12. After 2040 each such Sunday holiday needs a further dated entry, until urpx:mondayIfSundayObservance (proposed in urpx-org/urpx#77) can state the rule; the dated entries then come out. (4) Sheet 3's Detailed UDC Rates table decomposes the Base Services Charge into UDC sub-components (Distr 0.63391 + PPP 0.02913 + LGC 0.13039 = 0.79343 standard; 0.06674 + 0.00000 + 0.13039 = 0.19713 CARE; 0.23736 + 0.02913 + 0.13039 = 0.39688 DRAH and FERA). The model carries only the 0.79343 total, while decomposing the energy UDC into its published sub-components on the same table. The billed amount is unaffected, so this costs no accuracy today; it costs the ability to answer what share of the fixed charge is distribution. Trivially expressible (three more PriceDefinitions and Prices on the existing BSC ledger). Recorded here because it is real, but it is a corpus-wide convention rather than a DR-SES decision: every SDG&E base plan with a BSC ledger carries a single PriceDefinition on it, so settle it once for SDG&E rather than plan by plan. (5) General Special Condition 5 bars re-entry after leaving. Verbatim: \"If a customer elects to discontinue service on Schedule DR-SES, the customer will not be permitted to return to Schedule DR-SES for a period of 12 consecutive months.\" EECC Special Condition 3, carried into this schedule from the retired Schedule EECC, adds that a customer receiving optional service \"may elect to change to another applicable rate schedule, but only after receiving service on this Schedule for at least 12 consecutive months, except as specified in EECC Special Condition 4\", and bars return for one year unless returning from a Direct Access Provider or a CCA. The RatePlanVersion carries urpx:minimumTenure P12M, which the v0.5.1 ontology defines as \"The minimum duration a customer must remain enrolled in a rate plan, program, or service offering\"; from this version EECC Special Condition 3 supports it. Neither re-entry bar is modeled. The sibling ev-tou filing records its own re-entry bar in its deferrals.",
          "urpx:evaluatedOn": "2026-10-06T00:00:00"
        }
      }
    }
  }
